# Go build output. Anchored to the repository root: a bare `trainsty` pattern
# would also match a directory named trainsty at any depth.
/trainsty
/dist/

# `go mod vendor` output. Nothing should ever produce it — go.mod declares no
# dependencies (Principle I, and scripts/ci-local.sh enforces it) — so a vendor/
# directory appearing is a signal, not a thing to commit.
/vendor/

# Deliberately NOT ignoring *.exe: this project is Unix-only (ADR-002), and a
# pattern for a Windows artifact would imply a target that does not exist.

# Go test and coverage artefacts
*.test
*.out
coverage.*

# Local CI scratch — scripts/ci-local.sh caches nothing today, but a downloaded
# linter or a pinned binary would land here rather than in the tree.
.ci-cache/

# Agent-local settings. `.claude/skills/` IS tracked — the Spec Kit commands are
# part of the repository — and only the machine-specific settings are not.
.claude/settings.local.json

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editors
*.swp
.idea/
.vscode/
